{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":504976,"name":"Sam Smith","username":"Sam_Smith","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/sam_smith/{size}/122447_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-01T19:01:45.336Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHow do I share a custom MCP that one of my bots has built with the rest of my team?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-10-01T19:01:51.164Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":25.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":173538,"topic_slug":"how-do-i-share-a-custom-mcp-that-one-of-my-bots-has-built-with-the-rest-of-my-team","display_username":"Sam Smith","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135942,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/how-do-i-share-a-custom-mcp-that-one-of-my-bots-has-built-with-the-rest-of-my-team/173538/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":505060,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-01T21:24:46.283Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/sam_smith\"\u003e@Sam_Smith\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the question!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen one of your Bots adds an MCP server, it’s saved to your own account, so only you can use it. To share it, publish that Bot to your team and add the server to the Team Bot:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the Bot in the Grok Bot desktop app.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen its share menu and click \u003cstrong\u003ePublish to team\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOnce it’s published, open the Bot’s details and find its \u003cstrong\u003ePlugins\u003c/strong\u003e section.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick \u003cstrong\u003eAdd plugins\u003c/strong\u003e, then \u003cstrong\u003eAdd custom\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnter the server’s URL (or command) and any secret values it needs.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEveryone who uses that Team Bot then gets the server. The setup is shared, but if the server signs in with an account, each teammate connects their own. You can also just ask the Bot, in your own chat with it, to add the server to itself after it’s published. One thing to check: if the MCP your Bot built runs as a local command from files on its own computer, your teammates’ sessions won’t have those files. Hosting it at a URL is the most reliable way to share it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s some images of the steps - I tried it out to make sure I was giving you the correct steps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/3/8/38a61ecbc017583669c9558141cdfa92acd64552.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/858EgrtG1XmR3Tkwk9AP4gvSVMe.png?dl=1\" title=\"SCR-20261001-mucl-2\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/8/38a61ecbc017583669c9558141cdfa92acd64552_2_426x499.png\" alt=\"SCR-20261001-mucl-2\" data-base62-sha1=\"858EgrtG1XmR3Tkwk9AP4gvSVMe\" width=\"426\" height=\"499\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/8/38a61ecbc017583669c9558141cdfa92acd64552_2_426x499.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/3/8/38a61ecbc017583669c9558141cdfa92acd64552_2_639x748.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/3/8/38a61ecbc017583669c9558141cdfa92acd64552.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F5F6F6\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eSCR-20261001-mucl-2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e677×794 30.6 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/b/c/bcaa9852494014c0b95f4dd1b7223dfa61bedbc0.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/qV1ghgYEYQHPvXTvrIWoUX5KP1S.png?dl=1\" title=\"SCR-20261001-mupo\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/c/bcaa9852494014c0b95f4dd1b7223dfa61bedbc0_2_690x326.png\" alt=\"SCR-20261001-mupo\" data-base62-sha1=\"qV1ghgYEYQHPvXTvrIWoUX5KP1S\" width=\"690\" height=\"326\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/c/bcaa9852494014c0b95f4dd1b7223dfa61bedbc0_2_690x326.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/c/bcaa9852494014c0b95f4dd1b7223dfa61bedbc0_2_1035x489.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/b/c/bcaa9852494014c0b95f4dd1b7223dfa61bedbc0_2_1380x652.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F3F3F3\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eSCR-20261001-mupo\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1984×940 87.7 KB\u003c/span